-- ccc10-hate.l4 -- sections 318 to 320.1 of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46: hate propaganda (advocating genocide, public incitement of hatred,
-- wilful promotion of hatred and of antisemitism, hate symbols, their defences, forfeiture, and the warrants of seizure and orders of deletion).
-- Layer 1 (the law, objectively).
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30).
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
-- How a result reads: JUST TRUE (every element holds, or the defence or duty applies); JUST FALSE (the text says no in its own words, quoted in the branch's comment);
-- NOTHING (not covered: an element is missing, the text is silent or limits a grant or prohibition in its own wording, or the answer points outside the text).
-- A caller never turns NOTHING into FALSE. Seams: `s 83.01(1) listed entity` is ccc3's; `s 787(1) ...` is ccc29's; `s 2 Attorney General` (who consents) is a plain fact here.

§ `s 318 -- Advocating genocide`

-- src:6019 | 318 (1) Every person who advocates or promotes genocide is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than five years.
@ref s 318(1) (src:6019)
GIVEN `the person advocates or promotes genocide` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 318(1) the person is guilty of the offence of advocating genocide` MEANS
    IF `the person advocates or promotes genocide`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every person who advocates or promotes genocide is guilty of an indictable offence"

@ref s 318(1) (src:6019)
`s 318(1) the class of the offence` MEANS `an indictable offence`

@ref s 318(1) (src:6019)
`s 318(1) the punishment` MEANS Punishment OF `by indictment`, (`imprisonment for a term of` `five years`), `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

-- 318(2): "genocide means" acts committed with intent to destroy an identifiable group: closed.
-- src:6020 | Definition of genocide
-- src:6021 | (2) In this section, genocide means any of the following acts committed with intent to destroy in whole or in part any identifiable group, namely,
-- src:6022 | (a) killing members of the group; or
-- src:6023 | (b) deliberately inflicting on the group conditions of life calculated to bring about its physical destruction.
@ref s 318(2) (src:6020-6023)
GIVEN `the act is killing members of the group` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act is deliberately inflicting on the group conditions of life calculated to bring about its physical destruction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act is committed with intent to destroy in whole or in part any identifiable group` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 318(2) the act is genocide` MEANS
    IF `the act is committed with intent to destroy in whole or in part any identifiable group` AND (`the act is killing members of the group` OR `the act is deliberately inflicting on the group conditions of life calculated to bring about its physical destruction`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "genocide means any of the following acts committed with intent to destroy in whole or in part any identifiable group" (a "means" definition)

-- 318(3): a bar: no proceeding without the Attorney General's consent. With consent the bar is lifted and the text says nothing further (fork F29).
