-- src:6026 | Definition of identifiable group
-- src:6027 | (4) In this section, identifiable group means any section of the public distinguished by colour, race, religion, national or ethnic origin, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or mental or physical disability.
@ref s 318(4) (src:6026-6027)
GIVEN `the group is a section of the public` IS A BOOLEAN
      ground IS A `s 318(4) the ground by which the section of the public is distinguished`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 318(4) the section of the public is an identifiable group` MEANS
    IF `the group is a section of the public` AND (NOT (ground EQUALS `s 318(4) another ground`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "identifiable group means any section of the public distinguished by colour, race, religion, national or ethnic origin, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or mental or physical disability" (a "means" definition)

§ `s 319 -- Public incitement of hatred and wilful promotion of hatred`

-- src:6029 | 319 (1) Every one who, by communicating statements in any public place, incites hatred against any identifiable group where such incitement is likely to lead to a breach of the peace is guilty of
-- src:6030 | (a) an indictable offence and is liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding two years; or
-- src:6031 | (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 319(1) (src:6029-6031)
GIVEN `the person communicates statements in any public place` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person incites hatred against any identifiable group` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the incitement is likely to lead to a breach of the peace` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 319(1) the person is guilty of the offence of public incitement of hatred` MEANS
    IF `the person communicates statements in any public place` AND `the person incites hatred against any identifiable group` AND `the incitement is likely to lead to a breach of the peace`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by communicating statements in any public place, incites hatred against any identifiable group where such incitement is likely to lead to a breach of the peace"

@ref s 319(1) (src:6029-6031)
`s 319(1) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

@ref s 319(1) (src:6030-6031)
GIVEN mode IS A `Mode of proceeding`
      `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
