-- 319(2.2): hate symbols. The listed entity is s 83.01(1)'s (ccc3), an input of type MAYBE BOOLEAN.
-- src:6040 | Wilful promotion of hatred — terrorism and hate symbols
-- src:6041 | (2.2) Everyone commits an offence who wilfully promotes hatred against any identifiable group by displaying, in any public place,
-- src:6042 | (a) a symbol that is principally used by, or principally associated with, a listed entity, as defined in subsection 83.01(1);
-- src:6043 | (b) the Nazi Hakenkreuz, the Nazi double Sig-Rune, also known as the SS bolts, or a noose; or
-- src:6044 | (c) a symbol that so nearly resembles a symbol described in paragraph (a) or (b) that it is likely to be a symbol described in paragraph (a) or (b).
@ref s 319(2.2) (src:6040-6044)
GIVEN `the person wilfully promotes hatred against any identifiable group` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person does so by displaying a symbol in a public place` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 83.01(1) listed entity: the symbol is principally used by, or principally associated with, a listed entity` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the symbol is the Nazi Hakenkreuz, the Nazi double Sig-Rune, also known as the SS bolts, or a noose` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the symbol so nearly resembles a symbol described in paragraph (a) or (b) that it is likely to be a symbol described in paragraph (a) or (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 319(2.2) the person commits the offence of wilful promotion of hatred by displaying a symbol` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the person wilfully promotes hatred against any identifiable group` AND `the person does so by displaying a symbol in a public place`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Everyone commits an offence who wilfully promotes hatred against any identifiable group by displaying, in any public place"
        IF (`s 83.01(1) listed entity: the symbol is principally used by, or principally associated with, a listed entity` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR `the symbol is the Nazi Hakenkreuz, the Nazi double Sig-Rune, also known as the SS bolts, or a noose` OR `the symbol so nearly resembles a symbol described in paragraph (a) or (b) that it is likely to be a symbol described in paragraph (a) or (b)` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `s 83.01(1) listed entity: the symbol is principally used by, or principally associated with, a listed entity` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the entity is a listed entity is for s 83.01(1) and is not determined
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(a) a symbol that is principally used by, or principally associated with, a listed entity ... (b) the Nazi Hakenkreuz ... or a noose; or (c) a symbol that so nearly resembles"

