-- 319(4): "may ... be ordered ... to be forfeited": a grant with an "If" gate: a failed gate gives NOTHING (the 2026-11-12 ruling, limit (1); fork F4).
-- src:6065 | Forfeiture
-- src:6066 | (4) If a person is convicted of an offence under subsection (1), (2), (2.1) or (2.2) or section 318, anything by means of or in relation to which the offence was committed, on such conviction, may, in addition to any other punishment imposed, be ordered by the presiding provincial court judge or judge to be forfeited to His Majesty in right of the province in which that person is convicted, for disposal as the Attorney General may direct.
@ref s 319(4) (src:6065-6066)
GIVEN offence IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `the person is convicted of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing is anything by means of or in relation to which the offence was committed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 319(4) the presiding judge may order the thing to be forfeited to His Majesty in right of the province` MEANS
    IF `the person is convicted of the offence` AND `the thing is anything by means of or in relation to which the offence was committed`
       AND (   (offence's `section` EQUALS 319 AND (offence's `subsection` EQUALS "(1)" OR offence's `subsection` EQUALS "(2)" OR offence's `subsection` EQUALS "(2.1)" OR offence's `subsection` EQUALS "(2.2)"))
            OR offence's `section` EQUALS 318)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If a person is convicted of an offence under subsection (1), (2), (2.1) or (2.2) or section 318, anything by means of or in relation to which the offence was committed, on such conviction, may, in addition to any other punishment imposed, be ordered by the presiding provincial court judge or judge to be forfeited"

DECLARE `s 319(4) the act of the judge` IS ONE OF `s 319(4) order the thing to be forfeited to His Majesty in right of the province`

@ref s 319(4) (src:6065-6066)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 319(4) the act of the judge`
`s 319(4) the permission of the judge` MEANS
    PARTY `a judge`
    MAY `s 319(4) order the thing to be forfeited to His Majesty in right of the province`
    HENCE FULFILLED

