§ `s 320 -- Warrant of seizure`

-- src:6082 | 320 (1) A judge who is satisfied by information on oath that there are reasonable grounds for believing that any publication, copies of which are kept for sale or distribution in premises within the jurisdiction of the court, is hate propaganda shall issue a warrant under his hand authorizing seizure of the copies.
@ref s 320(1) (src:6082)
GIVEN `the judge is satisfied by information on oath that there are reasonable grounds for believing that the publication is hate propaganda` IS A BOOLEAN
      `copies of the publication are kept for sale or distribution in premises within the jurisdiction of the court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320(1) the judge shall issue a warrant under his hand authorizing seizure of the copies` MEANS
    IF `the judge is satisfied by information on oath that there are reasonable grounds for believing that the publication is hate propaganda` AND `copies of the publication are kept for sale or distribution in premises within the jurisdiction of the court`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A judge who is satisfied by information on oath that there are reasonable grounds for believing that any publication, copies of which are kept for sale or distribution in premises within the jurisdiction of the court, is hate propaganda shall issue a warrant" (a failed gate: marginal reading (a))

DECLARE `s 320(1) the act of the judge` IS ONE OF `s 320(1) issue a warrant under his hand authorizing seizure of the copies`

@ref s 320(1) (src:6082)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 320(1) the act of the judge`
`s 320(1) the duty of the judge to issue the warrant` MEANS
    PARTY `a judge`
    MUST `s 320(1) issue a warrant under his hand authorizing seizure of the copies`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `a judge` BECAUSE "no warrant was issued although the judge was satisfied by information on oath"

-- src:6083 | Summons to occupier
-- src:6084 | (2) Within seven days of the issue of a warrant under subsection (1), the judge shall issue a summons to the occupier of the premises requiring him to appear before the court and show cause why the matter seized should not be forfeited to Her Majesty.
@ref s 320(2) (src:6083-6084)
GIVEN `the day on which the warrant under subsection (1) was issued` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the judge issued the summons to the occupier` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320(2) the judge issued the summons to the occupier within seven days of the issue of the warrant` MEANS
    IF (DATE_SERIAL `the day on which the judge issued the summons to the occupier`) MINUS (DATE_SERIAL `the day on which the warrant under subsection (1) was issued`) AT MOST 7
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Within seven days of the issue of a warrant under subsection (1), the judge shall issue a summons to the occupier of the premises" (a period the text fixes in its own words: ruling of 2026-11-05 (a))

DECLARE `s 320(2) the act of the judge` IS ONE OF `s 320(2) issue a summons to the occupier of the premises requiring him to appear before the court and show cause why the matter seized should not be forfeited to Her Majesty`

@ref s 320(2) (src:6083-6084)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 320(2) the act of the judge`
`s 320(2) the duty of the judge to issue the summons within seven days` MEANS
    PARTY `a judge`
    MUST `s 320(2) issue a summons to the occupier of the premises requiring him to appear before the court and show cause why the matter seized should not be forfeited to Her Majesty`
    WITHIN 7   -- days, counted from the issue of the warrant (the trace starts at that day, AT 0)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `a judge` BECAUSE "no summons was issued to the occupier within seven days of the issue of the warrant"

