    IF `the court is not satisfied that the publication referred to in subsection (1) is hate propaganda`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the court is not satisfied that the publication referred to in subsection (1) is hate propaganda, it shall order that the matter be restored" (a failed "If": marginal reading (a))

@ref s 320(5) (src:6089-6090)
GIVEN `the court is not satisfied that the publication referred to in subsection (1) is hate propaganda` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the time for final appeal has expired` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320(5) the matter cannot yet be restored until the time for final appeal has expired` MEANS
    IF NOT `the court is not satisfied that the publication referred to in subsection (1) is hate propaganda`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the court is not satisfied that the publication referred to in subsection (1) is hate propaganda, it shall order that the matter be restored"
    ELSE IF `the time for final appeal has expired`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "forthwith after the time for final appeal has expired" (the time has expired: the bar is over)
         ELSE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `s 320(5) the act of the court` IS ONE OF `s 320(5) order that the matter be restored to the person from whom it was seized`

@ref s 320(5) (src:6089-6090)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 320(5) the act of the court`
