DECLARE `s 320(6) the ground of appeal` IS ONE OF
    `s 320(6)(a) a question of law alone`
    `s 320(6)(b) a question of fact alone`
    `s 320(6)(c) a question of mixed law and fact`
    `s 320(6) a ground of another kind`

-- src:6091 | Appeal
-- src:6092 | (6) An appeal lies from an order made under subsection (4) or (5) by any person who appeared in the proceedings
-- src:6093 | (a) on any ground of appeal that involves a question of law alone,
-- src:6094 | (b) on any ground of appeal that involves a question of fact alone, or
-- src:6095 | (c) on any ground of appeal that involves a question of mixed law and fact,
-- src:6096 | as if it were an appeal against conviction or against a judgment or verdict of acquittal, as the case may be, on a question of law alone under Part XXI, and sections 673 to 696 apply with such modifications as the circumstances require.
@ref s 320(6) (src:6091-6096)
GIVEN `the order was made under subsection (4) or (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appellant is a person who appeared in the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
      ground IS A `s 320(6) the ground of appeal`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320(6) an appeal lies from the order` MEANS
    IF `the order was made under subsection (4) or (5)` AND `the appellant is a person who appeared in the proceedings` AND (NOT (ground EQUALS `s 320(6) a ground of another kind`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An appeal lies from an order made under subsection (4) or (5) by any person who appeared in the proceedings (a) on any ground of appeal that involves a question of law alone, (b) ... fact alone, or (c) ... mixed law and fact"

@ref s 320(6) closing words (src:6096)
GIVEN `the order was made under subsection (4) or (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320(6) sections 673 to 696 apply with such modifications as the circumstances require` MEANS
    IF `the order was made under subsection (4) or (5)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "as if it were an appeal against conviction or against a judgment or verdict of acquittal, as the case may be, on a question of law alone under Part XXI, and sections 673 to 696 apply with such modifications as the circumstances require" (the sections are ccc24's)

