-- src:6110 | hate propaganda means any writing, sign or visible representation that advocates or promotes genocide or the communication of which by any person would constitute an offence under section 319; (propagande haineuse)
@ref s 320(8) hate propaganda (src:6110)
GIVEN `it is a writing, sign or visible representation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it advocates or promotes genocide` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the communication of it by any person would constitute an offence under section 319` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320(8) the matter is hate propaganda` MEANS
    IF `it is a writing, sign or visible representation` AND (`it advocates or promotes genocide` OR `the communication of it by any person would constitute an offence under section 319`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "hate propaganda means any writing, sign or visible representation that advocates or promotes genocide or the communication of which by any person would constitute an offence under section 319" (a "means" definition)

