    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "judge means a judge of a court" (a "means" definition)

§ `s 320.1 -- Warrant of seizure (computer system)`

-- 320.1(1): "the judge may order": a grant with an "If" gate: a failed gate gives NOTHING (limit (1) of 2026-11-12; fork F4).
-- src:6113 | 320.1 (1) If a judge is satisfied by information on oath that there are reasonable grounds to believe that there is material that is hate propaganda within the meaning of subsection 320(8) or computer data within the meaning of subsection 342.1(2) that makes hate propaganda available, that is stored on and made available to the public through a computer system within the meaning of subsection 342.1(2) that is within the jurisdiction of the court, the judge may order the custodian of the computer system to
-- src:6114 | (a) give an electronic copy of the material to the court;
-- src:6115 | (b) ensure that the material is no longer stored on and made available through the computer system; and
-- src:6116 | (c) provide the information necessary to identify and locate the person who posted the material.
@ref s 320.1(1) (src:6113-6116)
GIVEN `the judge is satisfied by information on oath that there are reasonable grounds to believe that there is material that is hate propaganda, or computer data that makes hate propaganda available, stored on and made available to the public through a computer system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the computer system is within the jurisdiction of the court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.1(1) the judge may order the custodian of the computer system to give an electronic copy, ensure the material is no longer available, and identify the person who posted it` MEANS
    IF `the judge is satisfied by information on oath that there are reasonable grounds to believe that there is material that is hate propaganda, or computer data that makes hate propaganda available, stored on and made available to the public through a computer system` AND `the computer system is within the jurisdiction of the court`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If a judge is satisfied by information on oath that there are reasonable grounds to believe that there is material that is hate propaganda ... that is within the jurisdiction of the court, the judge may order the custodian of the computer system to"

DECLARE `s 320.1(1) the act of the judge` IS ONE OF `s 320.1(1) order the custodian of the computer system to give an electronic copy of the material to the court, ensure that the material is no longer stored on and made available through the computer system, and provide the information necessary to identify and locate the person who posted the material`

@ref s 320.1(1) (src:6113-6116)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 320.1(1) the act of the judge`
`s 320.1(1) the permission of the judge` MEANS
    PARTY `a judge`
    MAY `s 320.1(1) order the custodian of the computer system to give an electronic copy of the material to the court, ensure that the material is no longer stored on and made available through the computer system, and provide the information necessary to identify and locate the person who posted the material`
    HENCE FULFILLED

-- src:6117 | Notice to person who posted the material
-- src:6118 | (2) Within a reasonable time after receiving the information referred to in paragraph (1)(c), the judge shall cause notice to be given to the person who posted the material, giving that person the opportunity to appear and be represented before the court and show cause why the material should not be deleted. If the person cannot be identified or located or does not reside in Canada, the judge may order the custodian of the computer system to post the text of the notice at the location where the material was previously stored and made available, until the time set for the appearance.
@ref s 320.1(2) (src:6117-6118)
GIVEN `the judge has received the information referred to in paragraph (1)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice was given within a reasonable time after receiving it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.1(2) the judge shall cause notice to be given to the person who posted the material` MEANS
    IF NOT `the judge has received the information referred to in paragraph (1)(c)`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Within a reasonable time after receiving the information referred to in paragraph (1)(c)"
    ELSE IF `the notice was given within a reasonable time after receiving it`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Within a reasonable time after receiving the information referred to in paragraph (1)(c), the judge shall cause notice to be given" (a period the text fixes in its own words; whether the time is reasonable is the court's judgment, a plain input)

@ref s 320.1(2) (src:6117-6118)
GIVEN `the person cannot be identified or located or does not reside in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.1(2) the judge may order the custodian to post the text of the notice` MEANS
    IF `the person cannot be identified or located or does not reside in Canada`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the person cannot be identified or located or does not reside in Canada, the judge may order the custodian of the computer system to post the text of the notice"

