    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the person who posted the material does not appear for the proceedings, the court may proceed ex parte"

-- src:6123 | Order
-- src:6124 | (5) If the court is satisfied, on a balance of probabilities, that the material is available to the public and is hate propaganda within the meaning of subsection 320(8) or computer data within the meaning of subsection 342.1(2) that makes hate propaganda available, it may order the custodian of the computer system to delete the material.
@ref s 320.1(5) (src:6123-6124)
GIVEN `the court is satisfied, on a balance of probabilities, that the material is available to the public and is hate propaganda or computer data that makes hate propaganda available` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.1(5) the court may order the custodian of the computer system to delete the material` MEANS
    IF `the court is satisfied, on a balance of probabilities, that the material is available to the public and is hate propaganda or computer data that makes hate propaganda available`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the court is satisfied, on a balance of probabilities, that the material is available to the public and is hate propaganda ... it may order the custodian of the computer system to delete the material"

-- 320.1(6): "When the court makes the order ..., it may order the destruction": a "may" with a "When" gate: JUST FALSE outside it, ruling (b) of 2026-11-05, listed for a lawyer in fork F46.
-- src:6125 | Destruction of copy
-- src:6126 | (6) When the court makes the order for the deletion of the material, it may order the destruction of the electronic copy in the court’s possession.
@ref s 320.1(6) (src:6125-6126)
GIVEN `the court makes the order for the deletion of the material` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.1(6) the court may order the destruction of the electronic copy in the court’s possession` MEANS
    IF `the court makes the order for the deletion of the material`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "When the court makes the order for the deletion of the material, it may order the destruction of the electronic copy in the court’s possession" (a failed "When": ruling of 2026-11-05 (b); F46)

-- src:6127 | Return of material
-- src:6128 | (7) If the court is not satisfied that the material is available to the public and is hate propaganda within the meaning of subsection 320(8) or computer data within the meaning of subsection 342.1(2) that makes hate propaganda available, the court shall order that the electronic copy be returned to the custodian and terminate the order under paragraph (1)(b).
@ref s 320.1(7) (src:6127-6128)
GIVEN `the court is not satisfied that the material is available to the public and is hate propaganda or computer data that makes hate propaganda available` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.1(7) the court shall order that the electronic copy be returned to the custodian and terminate the order under paragraph (1)(b)` MEANS
    IF `the court is not satisfied that the material is available to the public and is hate propaganda or computer data that makes hate propaganda available`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the court is not satisfied that the material is available to the public and is hate propaganda ... the court shall order that the electronic copy be returned" (a failed "If": marginal reading (a))

-- src:6129 | Other provisions to apply
-- src:6130 | (8) Subsections 320(6) to (8) apply, with any modifications that the circumstances require, to this section.
@ref s 320.1(8) (src:6129-6130)
GIVEN `the question is asked about a proceeding under section 320.1` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.1(8) subsections 320(6) to (8) apply to the proceeding` MEANS
    IF `the question is asked about a proceeding under section 320.1`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subsections 320(6) to (8) apply, with any modifications that the circumstances require, to this section"

-- 320.1(9): "takes effect until": an "until" bar (ruling (d)): the order cannot yet take effect until the time for final appeal has expired.
-- src:6131 | When order takes effect
-- src:6132 | (9) No order made under subsections (5) to (7) takes effect until the time for final appeal has expired.
@ref s 320.1(9) (src:6131-6132)
GIVEN `the order was made under subsections (5) to (7)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the time for final appeal has expired` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.1(9) the order cannot yet take effect until the time for final appeal has expired` MEANS
    IF NOT `the order was made under subsections (5) to (7)`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "No order made under subsections (5) to (7)"
    ELSE IF `the time for final appeal has expired`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "takes effect until the time for final appeal has expired" (the time has expired: the bar is over)
         ELSE JUST TRUE
